{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"far-deistic-dowitcher","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Transition replay fallback for invalid direct Jira transitions\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nWhen rebar's target status is reachable in Jira only via intermediate states, the current\nreconciler attempts the direct end-state transition and, when Jira rejects it as illegal\n(handled around `dispatch_one.py` L402/445), the ticket drifts. But rebar records the\n*actual* hop sequence it took (e.g. open→in_progress→done); a Jira project that forbids\nopen→done directly may still allow open→in_progress→done. We want to replay rebar's real\nrecorded hops rather than give up on the first illegal direct transition. Self-healing\n(inventing hops Jira allows but rebar never took) was rejected; replay only mirrors hops\nthat actually happened in rebar.\n\n## Approach\n\nOn an illegal direct transition, fall back to **transition replay**: reconstruct rebar's\nrecorded status-hop sequence for the ticket, anchor on Jira's **current actual** status,\nand attempt each recorded hop in order using Jira's available-transitions API (the same\nAPI the direct path already queries). A hop is attempted only if it is (a) currently\navailable from Jira's present status and (b) has no un-fillable required field (no\nfield-guessing — a required field with no `create_defaults`/known value aborts). Any\nun-clean hop ⇒ fall back to **drift + warning** (today's terminal behavior). Replay is\nbest-effort and idempotent per pass: a partial advance is fine; the next pass re-anchors\non the new current status and continues. No new config axis — replay is behavior on the\nexisting transition path, gated by the S2 status mapping (each hop's target is resolved\nthrough the status map).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py` — replay fallback in the\n  illegal-transition branch (~L402/445).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_transition_replay.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Replay reaches end state (unit, faked transition API):** direct open→done is illegal\n  but open→in_progress and in_progress→done are available; assert both hops fire in order\n  and Jira reaches `done`.\n- **Un-clean hop drifts (failure path):** an intermediate hop is unavailable (or needs an\n  un-fillable required field); assert replay stops and the ticket drifts with a warning —\n  no partial-state crash, no field guessing.\n- **Re-anchor idempotence:** a second pass from a partially-advanced current status\n  continues from there rather than restarting — asserted on the hops attempted.\n- **No self-heal:** a hop rebar never recorded is never attempted even if Jira allows it —\n  asserted on the attempted-hop set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An illegal direct transition triggers replay of rebar's recorded hops, anchored on\n  Jira's current status, reaching the end state when every hop is clean — verified by\n  `test_transition_replay.py::test_replay_reaches_end_state`.\n- [ ] An un-clean hop (unavailable or un-fillable required field) falls back to drift +\n  warning with no field guessing — verified by\n  `test_transition_replay.py::test_unclean_hop_drifts`.\n- [ ] Replay re-anchors on current status and is idempotent across passes — verified by\n  `test_transition_replay.py::test_replay_reanchors`.\n- [ ] Only rebar-recorded hops are attempted (no self-heal) — verified by\n  `test_transition_replay.py::test_no_selfheal_hops`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit with a faked transition API** — the oracle is the ordered set\nof transition calls issued and the resulting status / drift alert; a live tier is\nunnecessary because the decision logic is what's under test, and the Jira transition API is\na narrow injected boundary.","id":"d458-bb1e-cc63-42a6","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Transition replay fallback for invalid direct Jira transitions"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787290326333999001,"uuid":"f0a71275-873e-482b-96f2-bb6cdb3b49d9"}